From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:43:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "cpufreq: Lower cpuinfo.max_freq again when software
 boost is disabled"

This reverts commit 5e12e584cf76a16357fa6fe7dd7dde3e5fceee76.

Test kernel 5 replaces the prep/hw-pm series with
prep/hw-pm-v5-tablemax-v2, which carries the reworked versions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqitcmCNS6G33aQUShi39x
---
 drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c
index 509dd6f..54dde84 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c
@@ -2802,12 +2802,6 @@ int cpufreq_boost_set_sw(struct cpufreq_policy *policy, int state)
 	if (!policy->freq_table)
 		return -ENXIO;
 
-	/*
-	 * cpufreq_frequency_table_cpuinfo() never lowers a cpuinfo.max_freq
-	 * set before it runs. Clear the limit so that disabling boost drops it
-	 * back to the highest non-boost frequency in the table.
-	 */
-	policy->cpuinfo.max_freq = 0;
 	ret = cpufreq_frequency_table_cpuinfo(policy);
 	if (ret)
 		pr_err("%s: Policy frequency update failed\n", __func__);
